(E) Exterior boundaries of superstructures and deckhouses enclosing accommodation and including any overhanging decks which support such accommodation shall be constructed of steel and insulated to 'A-60' standard for tM~ whole of the portions which face the cargo area and on the outward sides for a distance of 3 metres from the end boundary facing the cargo area. The distance of 3 metres shall be measured horizontally and parallel to the middle line of the ship from the boundary which faces the cargo area at each deck level. In the case of the sides of those superstructures and deckhouses, such insulation shall be carried up to the underside of the deck of the navigation bridge.

