(6) {a) In passenger ships carrying more than 36 passengers, the boundary bulkheads and decks of special category and ro-ro spaces shall be insulated to 'A-60' class standard. Where a category (5), (9) or (10) space, as defined in paragraph {b)(iii) of sub-regulation (2), is on one side of the division, the standard may be reduced to 'A-0'. Where fuel oil tanks are below a special category space, the integrity of the deck between such spaces may be reduced to 'A-0' standard.

